hadiths[91]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1285","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked which work is best? He said: “Faith in Allah and His Messenger.” It was said: “Then what?” He said: “Jihad for the sake of Allah.” It was said: “Then what?” He said: “An accepted Hajj.” ((Agreed) (on him)."
"1286","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, which work is most beloved to Allah Almighty? He said: “Prayer on time.” I said: Then what? He said: “Being kind to one’s parents.” I said: Then what: He said: “Jihad for the sake of Allah” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"1287","On the authority of Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, which work is better? He said: “Belief in Allah and jihad in His cause” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"1288","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A morning or a day in the path of Allah is better than this world and all that is in it” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"1289","A man came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said, \Who is the best among men?\"" He (ﷺ) replied"," \""A believer who strives in the way of Allah with his wealth and life.\"" The man asked again"," \""Who is next to him (in excellence)?\"" He (ﷺ) said"," \""Next to him is a man who is engaged in worshipping his Rubb in a mountain valley"," leaving the people secure from his mischief.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"1290","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \Observing Ribat (e.g."," guarding the Islamic frontier for the sake of Allah) for a single day is far better than the world and all that it contains. A place in Jannah as small as the whip of your horse is far better than the world and all that it contains. An endeavour (fighting) in the Cause of Allah in the evening or in the morning is far better than the world and all that it contains.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"1291","I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) as saying, \Observing Ribat in the way of Allah for a day and a night is far better than observing Saum (fasting) for a whole month and standing in Salat (prayer) in all its nights. If a person dies (while performing this duty)"," he will go on receiving his reward for his meritorious deeds perpetually"," and his sustenance is continually granted to him"," and he will be saved from Al- Fattan.\"" [Muslim] ."""
"1292","On the authority of Fadalah bin Ubaid, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Every dead person’s deeds are sealed, except those who are stationed in the path of Allah, for his deeds will be enhanced until the Day of Resurrection, and he will be safe from the trials of the grave” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]."
"1293","On the authority of Othman, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “A day’s bond in the path of Allah is better than a thousand days in other stations.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"1294","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah guarantees whoever goes out in His path. Only jihad in My path, faith in Me, and belief in My Messengers will take him out. He is upon me a guarantee that I will admit him to Paradise, or return him to his home from which he left with what he obtained of reward or spoils. By the One in Whose hand is Muhammad’s soul, no one who is wounded in the way of Allah will come on the Day of Resurrection in his form on the day he spoke.” Its color is the color of blood, and its smell is the smell of musk, and by the One in whose hand is Muhammad’s soul, were it not that it would be difficult for the Muslims, I would never have stayed behind a company that would fight in the path of Allah, but I do not find the capacity to carry them and they do not find the capacity for them to lag behind me. By the One in whose hand is Muhammad’s soul, I would like to fight in the path of Allah and be killed, then I would fight and be killed, then I would fight and be killed” [Narrated by Muslim and some of it was narrated by Al-Bukhari]. [“Speech” is the wound.]."
"1295","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \Whoever is wounded while fighting in the way of Allah"," will come on the Day of Resurrection with blood oozing from his wound having the colour of blood but with the fragrance of musk.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"1296","And on the authority of Muadh, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Any Muslim man who fights in the cause of Allah even for the interval between milking two she-camels is guaranteed Paradise, and whoever sustains a wound in the cause of Allah or suffers a catastrophe, it will come on the Day of Resurrection as abundant as it was: its color is saffron, and its scent is like musk” ([Abu Dawud]."
"1297","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man from among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by a mountain in which there was a spring of fresh water, and it pleased him. He said: If I were to isolate myself from the people and stay in this mountain, I will not do so until I ask permission from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). So he mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he said: “Do not do that, for the position of one of you in the path of Allah is better than his praying in his house for seventy years.” Would you like Allah to forgive you and admit you to Paradise? Fight in the path of Allah. Whoever fights in the path of Allah even for the interval between milking two she-camels, Paradise is guaranteed for him.” [Al-Tirmidhi]. [And “hicces”: what is between the two rings]."
"1298","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked: \What other good deed could be an equivalent of Jihad in the way of Allah?\"" He (ﷺ) replied"," \""You do not have the strength to do it.\"" (The narrator said:) The question was repeated twice or thrice"," but every time he (ﷺ) answered"," \""You do not have the strength to do it.\"" Then he (ﷺ) said"," \""One who goes out for Jihad in the Cause of Allah is like a person who observes Saum (fasting)"," stands in Salat (prayer) constantly"," recites the Ayat of the Qur'an and does not exhibit any lassitude in fasting and prayer until the participant of Jihad in the way of Allah returns.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"1299","On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Among the people’s best livelihood is a man holding the reins of his horse for the sake of Allah, flying on its back whenever he hears a shout, or a startled one flying on its back, seeking death or death in his place, or a man in possession of spoils or a peak of these peaks or the depth of one of these valleys who establishes prayer and pays zakat, and worships his Lord until certainty comes to him. There are none of the people except in “Good” [Muslim]."
"1300","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \In Jannah there are a hundred grades which Allah has prepared for those who fight in His Cause; and the distance between any two of those grades is like the distance between the heaven and the earth.\"" [Al-Bukhari] ."""
"1301","On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever is satisfied with Allah as his Lord and Islam as his religion, and with Muhammad as his Messenger, Paradise is guaranteed for him.” Abu Sa’id was amazed at her and said, “Repeat it to me, O Messenger of Allah.” So he returned it to him, then said: “And another by which Allah will raise the servant a hundred degrees in Paradise, and the distance between every two degrees is as between the heaven and the earth.” He said: And what is it? O Messenger of Allah? He said: “Jihad for the sake of Allah, jihad for the sake of Allah” [Muslim]."
"1302","On the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa Al-Ash’ari, he said: I heard my father, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was in the presence of the enemy, saying: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “The gates of Paradise are under the shade of swords.” Then a man of shabby appearance stood up and said, “O Abu Musa, did you hear the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say this?” He said: Yes, so he returned to his companions and said: “Recite peace be upon you.” Then he broke the sheath of his sword. So he threw it away, then walked with his sword to the enemy and struck him with it until he was killed” [Muslim]."
"1303","On the authority of Abu Abs Abd al-Rahman bin Jubair, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The feet of a servant that have become dusty in the cause of Allah will not be touched by the Fire” [Al-Bukhari]."
"1304","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A man who cries out of fear of Allah will not enter Hell until the milk returns in the udder, and dust for the sake of Allah and the smoke of Hell will not gather on a servant of Allah” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"1305","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Two eyes that are not touched by fire are an eye that wept out of fear of Allah, and an eye that spent the night guarding in the path of Allah” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"1306","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \He who equips a Ghazi (fighter) in the way of Allah is as if he has taken part in the fighting himself; and he who looks after the dependants of a Ghazi in his absence"," is as if he has taken part in the fighting himself.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"1307","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \The best of charities is to provide canopy in the Cause of Allah"," to give a servant as a gift in the way of Allah"," and to provide a camel in the way of Allah (to be used by a Mujahid).\"" [At-Tirmidhi] ."""
"1308","And on the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that a young man from Aslam said: O Messenger of Allah, I want to fight and I do not have what to prepare with. He said: “Come so-and-so. He was preparing and fell ill, so he came to him and said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) greets you and says: Give me what you have prepared. He said: O so-and-so, give him what you prepared with, and do not withhold anything from him. By Allah, do not withhold anything from him.” May He bless you for it [Muslim]."
"1309","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent an expedition to Banu Lahyan and said, \One man from every two should join the fighting force"," and the reward is between them.\"" [Muslim] . Another narration in Muslim is: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"," \""Let one of every two men go forth\"""," and added: \""Whoever stays behind (and looks well after the family and the property of those who have joined the expedition) will get half the reward of the warrior.\"""""
"1310","On the authority of Al-Baraa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man clad in iron armor came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and he said, O Messenger of Allah, should I fight or become a Muslim? He said: “Become a Muslim, then fight.” So he became a Muslim, then he fought and was killed. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Work a little and be rewarded a lot” [Agreed upon, and this is the wording of Al-Bukhari]."
"1311","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “No one who enters Paradise wishes to return to this world, even if he had everything on earth, except the martyr, who He wishes to return to this world and be killed ten times for the dignity he sees.”"
"1312","On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah forgives the martyr everything except debt” [Muslim]."
"1313","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood up among his Companions and said, \Jihad in the way of Allah and belief in Allah (with all His Attributes) are the most meritorious of actions.\"" A man stood up and said: \""O Messenger of Allah! Inform me if I am killed in the way of Allah"," will my sins be blotted out?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"," \""Yes"," in case you are killed in the way of Allah and you remained patient"," hopeful of reward"," and advancing forward without retracing back (i.e."," while fighting).\"" Then he said"," \""What was your question?\"" He inquired again: \""Inform me"," if I am killed in the way of Allah"," will all my sins be blotted out?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) replied"," \""If you remained patient"," hopeful of reward and always fought without turning your back upon enemy"," everything"," except debt"," will be forgiven. Jibril has told me this.\"" [Muslim] ."""
"1314","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man said: Where will I be, O Messenger of Allah, if I am killed? He said: “In Paradise.” So he threw dates that were in his hand, then fought until he was killed. [Muslim]."
"1315","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and his companions set out until they preceded the polytheists to Badr. The polytheists came, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “None of you should approach anything until I am ahead of him.” So the polytheists approached, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Arise to a garden as wide as the heavens and the earth.” He said: Umair ibn al-Hammam says: Al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him: O Messenger of Allah, a paradise as wide as the heavens and the earth? He said: “Yes.” He said: “Bakh, bakh.” Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “What makes you say, “Bakh, bakh?” He said, “You are one of its people.” So he took out dates from his bag and began to eat some of them. Then he said, “If I live to eat these dates of mine, it will be a long life!” So he threw away what he had with him. dates, then fought them until he was killed” [Muslim]. (4)"
"1316","On his authority, he said: People came to the Prophet (ﷺ) asking him to send men with us who would teach us the Qur’an and the Sunnah. So he sent to them seventy men from the Ansar who were called the reciters. Among them was my uncle Haram. They read the Qur’an and studied it at night, learning. During the day, they would bring water and put it in the mosque. They would collect firewood and sell it, and with it they would buy food for the people of Suffah and for the poor. So he sent them (ﷺ) and they presented themselves to them. So they killed them before they reached the place, and they said: Oh Allah, inform our Prophet that we have met you, and we have been satisfied with you, and you have been satisfied with us. A man came from behind Haram, Anas’s uncle and stabbed him with a spear until he pierced him through, and Haram said: You have won, by the Lord of the Kaaba. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “Your brothers have been killed, and they said: Oh Allah, inform our Prophet, we have met you, and we have been satisfied.” And you are satisfied with us.” (Agreed upon, and this is the Muslim wording.)"
"1317","My uncle Anas bin An- Nadr (May Allah be pleased with him) was absent from the battle of Badr. He said: \O Messenger of Allah! I was absent from the first battle you fought against the pagans. (By Allah!) if Allah gives me a chance to fight against the pagans"," no doubt"," Allah will see how (bravely) I will fight.\"" On the Day of Uhud"," when the Muslims turned their backs and fled"," he said"," \""O Allah! I apologize to You for what these (i.e."," his companions) have done"," and I denounce what these (i.e."," the pagans) have done.\"" Then he advanced and Sa'd bin Mu'adh met him. He said: \""O Sa'd bin Mu'adh! By the Rubb of An-Nadr"," Jannah! I am smelling its aroma coming from before (the mountain of) Uhud","\"" Later on"," Sa'd said: \""O Messenger of Allah! I cannot achieve or do what he (i.e."," Anas bin An-Nadr) did. We found more than eighty wounds by swords"," spears and arrows on his body. We found him dead and his body was mutilated so badly that none except his sister could recognise him by his finger.\"" We used to think that the following Ayah was revealed concerning him and other men of his sort: \""Among the believers are men who have been true to their covenant with Allah (i.e."," they have gone out for Jihad"," and showed not their backs to the disbelievers)"," of them some have fulfilled their obligations (i.e."," have been martyred).\"" (33:23)."""
"1318","On the authority of Samra, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Tonight I saw two men who came to me and took me up the tree and took me into a house that was the most excellent and best. I had never seen anything better than it. He said, ‘As for this house, it is the house of the martyrs.’” (5)"
"1319","Umm Ar-Rubaiy'i bint Al-Bara', who was the mother of Harithah bin Suraqah, came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \O Messenger of Allah! Will you not tell me about Harithah? (He was killed in the battle of Badr). If he is in Jannah I shall show endurance"," but if he has met another fate"," I may exert myself in weeping for him.\"" He (ﷺ) replied"," \""O mother of Harithah"," in in the gardens of Jannah there are many ranks"," and your son has attained Al-Firdaus"," the highest.\"" [Al- Bukhari] ."""
"1320","On the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: My father was brought to the Prophet (ﷺ) and he was mutilated and placed in his hands. So I went to uncover his face, but a group of people forbade me, and the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “The angels continue to shade him with their wings” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1321","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \He who supplicates Allah sincerely for martyrdom"," Allah will elevate him to the station of the martyrs"," even if he dies on his bed.\"" [Muslim] ."""
"1322","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \He who supplicates sincerely for martyrdom"," it will be granted to him even if it (martyrdom) does not befall him.\"" [Muslim] ."""
"1323","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \The martyr experiences no more pain in being slain than one of you experiences from the sting of a small bite.\"" [At-Tirmidhi] ."""
"1324","On the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Awfa, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on some of his days when he met the enemy, waited until the sun had set, then he rose among the people and said: “O people, do not wish to meet the enemy, and ask Allah for well-being. If you meet him, be patient, and know that Paradise is under the shade of swords.” Then he said: “O Allah, the sender of the Book and the conductor of the clouds, the defeater of the parties, defeat them and give us victory.” [Agreed upon]."
"1325","On the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There are two things that are not rejected, or rarely rejected: supplication at the call and at the time of battle, when they fight each other” [Abu Dawud]."
"1326","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) invaded, he would say: “O Allah, you are my support and my helper. By You I turn, by You I roam, by You I originate, and by You I fight” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]."
"1327","On the authority of Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, that when the Prophet (ﷺ) feared a people, he would say: “O Allah, we place you in their throats, and we seek refuge in you from their evils.” [Abu Dawud]."
"1328","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \There is goodness tied in the forelocks of horses till the Day of Resurrection.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"""
"1329","On the authority of Urwa Al-Barqi, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Horses have goodness tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection: reward and spoils” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"1330","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever keeps a horse for the sake of Allah out of faith in Allah and believing in His promise, its satiety, dung, and urine will be in his balance on the Day of Resurrection” [Al-Bukhari]."
"1331","On the authority of Abu Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) with a haltered she-camel, and he said: This is for the sake of Allah, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “You will have seven hundred she-camels on the Day of Resurrection, all of them mottled.” [Muslim]."
"1332","I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying from the pulpit, \Prepare to meet them (the enemy) with as much strength as you can afford. Verily! Strength is in archery"," strength is in archery"," strength is in archery.\"" [Muslim] ."""
"1333","I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying, \Lands shall be laid open to you"," and Allah will suffice you (against your enemies)"," so none of you will be unable to amuse yourselves with your arrows.\"" [Muslim] ."""
"1334","On his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever learns to practice archery (shoot arrows) and then abandons it is not one of us or has disobeyed” [Muslim]."
"1335","And on his authority, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “With one arrow, Allah admits three people into Paradise: the one who makes it and expects goodness in his work, the one who fletches the arrow and the one who shoots it. And shoot and ride, and that you shoot is dearer to me than that you ride. And whoever abandons shooting out of dislike for it, then he has abandoned a blessing.” Or he said: “he disbelieved in it.” [Abu Dawud]."
"1336","On the authority of Salamah bin Al-Akwa’, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) passed by a group of people practicing archery, and he said: “Aim at Banu Ishmael, for your father was an archer” [Al-Bukhari]."
"1337","On the authority of Amr bin Absa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: Whoever shoots an arrow for the sake of Allah will have a freed reward: [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]."
"1338","On the authority of Abu Yahya Khurraym bin Fatik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever spends in the way of Allah, it will be recorded for him seven hundred times” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"1339","On the authority of Abu Saeed, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There is no servant who fasts a day for the sake of Allah except that Allah, on that day, distances his face from the Fire by seventy years” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"1340","On the authority of Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Whoever fasts a day for the sake of Allah, Allah will place between him and Hell a ditch as between the sky and the earth” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"1341","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever dies without fighting, and does not talk to himself about the battle, dies on a branch of hypocrisy” [Muslim]."
"1342","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We were with the Prophet (ﷺ) on a campaign, and he said: “In Medina, there are men who, whenever you travel a distance or cross a valley, are with you and were confined by illness.”"
"1343","On the authority of Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, that a Bedouin came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man fights for spoils, a man fights to be remembered, and a man fights to see his place? And in one narration: He fights out of courage, and he fights in a feverish manner. And in a narration: And he fights in anger, so who is in the path of Allah? Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever fights so that the word of Allah may be supreme, is in the path of Allah” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1344","On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There is no raider or expeditionary force that invades, seizes spoils and is delivered, but they have hastened two-thirds of their rewards, and there is no raider or expeditionary force that fails or is injured except that their rewards have been fulfilled for them” [Muslim]."
"1345","A man sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to travel in the land. He (ﷺ) said to him, \Travel for my people is Jihad in the Cause of Allah"," the Mighty and Sublime.\"" [Abu Dawud] ."""
"1346","On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “Staying at home is like a battle” [Abu Dawud]."
"1347","When the Prophet (ﷺ) returned from the battle of Tabuk, people went out from Al-Madinah to meet him and I also met him with other children at Thaniyah-tul-Wada'. [Abu Dawud] ."
"1348","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, \He who neither takes part in fighting nor equips a warrior nor looks after his (the warrior's) family"," will be afflicted by severe calamities before the Day of Resurrection.\"" [Abu Dawud] ."""
"1349","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Strive the polytheists with your wealth, your souls, and your tongues” [Abu Dawud]."
"1350","On the authority of Abu Amr, and it is said: Abu Hakim al-Nu’man bin Muqrin, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) if he did not fight from the beginning of the day, he would delay fighting until the sun had set, the wind had blown, and victory had descended. [Narrated by Abu Dawud and al-Tirmidhi, and he said: a good and authentic hadith]."
"1351","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do not hope to meet the enemy, but if you meet him, be patient” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"1352","On his authority and on the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “War is a deception” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"1353","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Martyrs are five: the stabbed, the one who dies of abdominal disease, the drowned, the one who is destroyed, and the martyr for the sake of Allah” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"1354","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \Whom do you reckon to be martyr amongst you?\"" The Companions replied: \""The one who is killed in Allah's way.\"" He said"," \""In that case"," the martyrs among my people would be few.\"" The Companions asked: \""O Messenger of Allah! Then who are the martyrs?\"" He replied"," \""He who is killed in the way of Allah is a martyr; he who dies in the Cause of Allah is a martyr; he who dies of plague is a martyr; and he who dies of a belly disease is a martyr; and he who is drowned is a martyr.\"" [Muslim] . This Hadith shows the care Allah has for this Ummah"," which is the best Ummah of mankind. (Editor's Note)"""
"1355","On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever is killed while defending his property is a martyr” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"1356","On the authority of Abu Al-A'war Saeed bin Zaid bin Amr bin Nufayl, one of the ten people who were acclaimed for Paradise, may Allah be pleased with them, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Whoever is killed in defense of his money is a martyr, and whoever is killed in defense of his blood is a martyr, and whoever is killed in defense of his religion is a martyr, and whoever is killed in defense of his honor is a martyr” ([Abu Dawud]. True).."
"1357","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if a man comes and wants to take my money? He said: “Do not give him your money.” He said: What do you think if he fights me? He said: “Fight him.” He said: What do you think if he kills me? He said: “Then you are a martyr.” He said: What do you think if I kill him? He said: “He will be in Hell” [Muslim]."
"1358","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \He who sets free a Muslim slave"," Allah will deliver from the fire of Hell every limb of his body in return for every limb of the slave's body"," even his private parts.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"1359","On the authority of Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are best? He said: “Faith in Allah and jihad for the sake of Allah.” I said: Which slaves are best? He said: “The most precious ones are with their owners and the most valuable” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"1360","On the authority of Al-Ma’rour bin Suwayd, he said: I saw Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, wearing a robe and his boy had the same, so I asked him about that, and he mentioned that he had insulted a man during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he cursed him with his mother. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “You are a man of ignorance.” They are your brothers, and your slaves, Allah has placed them under your hands. Whoever has his brother under his hand. Let him feed him from what he eats and clothe him from what he wears, and do not burden them with anything that overwhelms them. If you burden them, then help them.” (Agreed upon)"
"1361","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “If one of you brings his servant his food, and if he does not make him sit with him, then let him give him a bite or two or a bite or two, for he is in charge of his treatment” [Al-Bukhari]. (9)"
"1362","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If a servant is sincere to his master and worships Allah well, he will have his reward twice” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"1363","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A slave who is owned and reconciled has two rewards, and by the One in Whose Hand is Abu Hurairah’s soul, had it not been for jihad in the path of Allah and Hajj, and honoring my mother, I would have loved to die while I was owned” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"1364","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \A slave who worships his Rubb (Allah) well and discharges efficiently and faithfully the duties which are assigned to him by his master"," will have a double reward.\"" [Al-Bukhari] ."""
"1365","On his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Three people have two rewards: a man from the People of the Book who believed in his Prophet, and believed in Muhammad, and the owned slave if he fulfilled the rights of Allah and the rights of his master, and a man who had a female slave who disciplined her well and taught her well and taught her well, then he freed her and married her, he has two rewards” (Agreed upon))"
"1366","On the authority of Maqil bin Yasar, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Worshiping in the midst of chaos is like a migration to me” [Muslim]."
"1367","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) to seek compensation for him, and he treated him harshly, so his companions treated him harshly, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Leave him, for the one who has the right has a say.” Then he said: “Give him a tooth similar to his own.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, we find nothing but a tooth better than his. He said: “Give him, for the best of you is the best of you.” Judge” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"1368","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “May Allah have mercy on a man who is tolerant when he sells, when he buys, and when he requires it” [Al-Bukhari]."
"1369","On the authority of Abu Qatada, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Whoever is pleased that Allah will save him from distress on the Day of Resurrection, let him relieve someone in difficulty or give up on his behalf” [Muslim]."
"1370","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There was a man who owed people debt, and he used to say to his young man: If you come in debt, forgive him. Perhaps Allah will forgive us. So he met Allah and he will forgive him.” (Agreed upon)"
"1371","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \A person from amongst the people who lived before you was called to account by Allah on the Day of Resurrection. No good deeds were found in his credit except that he being a rich man had (financial) dealings with people and had commanded his servants to show leniency to those who were in straitened circumstances. Upon this Allah"," the Exalted"," and Majestic said: 'I am more entitled to this attribute"," so waive (his faults).\""' [Muslim] ."""
"1372","And on the authority of Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Allah Almighty brought a servant of His servants to whom Allah gave money, and He said to him: What did you do in the world? He said: And do not conceal anything from Allah - He said: O Lord, you have given me your money, so I used to trade with people, and leniency was my character, so I used to facilitate the wealthy and give respite to the debtor, so Allah Almighty said: “I am more deserving of this than you, so waive his faults.” Uqba said. Bin Amer and Abu Masoud Al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with them. This is how we heard it from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). [Muslim]."
"1373","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever provides relief to a distressed person or eases his debt, Allah will shade him on the Day of Resurrection under the shade of His Throne on a day when there will be no shade except His shade.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"1374","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) bought a camel from him and weighed it, so he made the scale heavier. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"1375","On the authority of Abu Safwan Suwayd bin Qays, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Me and Makhramah al-Abdi brought fine linen from Hijr, so the Prophet (ﷺ) came to us and bargained with us for trousers, and I had a weigher who weighed for a reward. The Prophet (ﷺ) said to the weigher, “Weigh and make heavier.” [Abu Dawud]"
